        "At Dusan’s call, men leapt to action, their instincts sharpened by drills. Dropping mugs and half-eaten plates, soldiers and sailors scrambled into position. Some scurried below deck, while others readied weapons and took cover by the ship’s railings or cargo. A few fumbled, caught halfway between celebration and catastrophe, the ale still fresh on their breath.",
