        "Jelert’s heart drummed in his chest. The hilt of the small sword was too short for his two-handed grip, but he couldn’t let go. His fists clenched awkwardly over each other, straining against the narrow space. The clashing of steel, shouting of curses, and sounds of death filled the air, all but drowned out by the pounding of blood in his ears.",
        "Flashes erupted across the deck as the brightshields converted each blow into bursts of radiance. Jelert focused on the mechanics: the shields converted kinetic energy, releasing it harmlessly as light. They were designed to endure the punishment of multiple engagements. That meant they’d hold—they had to.",
        "A brilliant blaze nearby filled Jelert’s vision, and he squeezed his eyes shut.",
        "When he opened them, only the two soldiers remained—Dusan was gone.",
        "A battle line had formed on the deck, an expanding bubble of attackers pushing out from where they’d boarded the ship. No longer distant shapes in the dark, the attackers were now close enough to see in detail. They advanced in formation, covering one another, responding to shouted commands.",
        "Something wasn’t adding up.",
        "Jelert clung to the details, forcing his mind to work through the chaos.",
        "These weren’t pirates—pirates didn’t move like this. Pirates embraced chaos from the outset, relying on individual daring rather than cohesive formations. These attackers moved as a unit, taking orders from a figure at their center. They were soldiers, trained, organized.",
