        "A brightshield flared in the distance, drawing Jelert’s eye. It was Dusan, leading a charge into the enemy. With a battle cry, he struck down the man before him and rushed forward, his soldiers at his sides. The enemy line buckled. The raiders fell back, some scrambling down their grappling ropes, others leaping the distance to the deck of the smaller vessel.",
        "Moments later, their lightless ship slipped away into the night.",
        "“No point in chasing them,” the captain said, breathing heavily as he surveyed the aftermath. “This fat tub can’t follow them into the shallows. We’ll wreck her on the rocks before we get anywhere near them.” He glanced at Jelert, still huddled in the corner, and shook his head before walking off, issuing orders to tend the wounded, inventory the stolen materials, and clean up the deck.",
        "A few minutes later, Jelert stood where he'd been eating his meal only a quarter hour ago. He was unable to tear his eyes from one fallen soldier, Mirek, on his side with his spear still grasped in both hands. The dead man’s eyes were anchored to the weapon.",
        "“Are you alright, Major?” Dusan’s voice dissipated the fog. The glow of the lanterns cast a grim, almost feral light on his blood-streaked features.",
